<title>USA: United seeks probe of British Air-American deal.</title>
<headline>United seeks probe of British Air-American deal.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Airlines said Wednesday it filed a request with the U.S. Department of Transportation (DOT) to begin a formal investigation of the alliance between British Airways Plc and AMR Corp's American Airlines.</p>
<p>United is owned by UAL Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;At present there is no U.S. forum for comment on the BA - American alliance,&quot; Stuart Oran, United Airlines executive vice president and general counsel, said in a statement. &quot;A formal DOT investigation would allow the U.S. to develop an informed policy on the alliance rather than reacting to the conclusions made by regulators investigating it for the U.K. and the (European Union).&quot;</p>
<p>Oran called upon DOT to immediately implement the investigation to allow ample time for negotiation with the United Kingdom and the European Union to resolve any conflicts that might arise.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
